# Expo / CNG (Continuous Native Generation) workflow
#
# android/ and ios/ are deliberately NOT committed — this project is fully
# managed (app.json is the single source of truth for native config).
# Committing those folders would make EAS Build treat this as a "bare"
# workflow and skip running `expo prebuild` automatically, which is
# exactly the "app config fields may not be synced" warning `expo-doctor`
# flagged: any future change to orientation/icon/scheme/splash/ios/
# android/plugins in app.json would silently stop taking effect on the
# next build. Regenerate locally anytime with `npx expo prebuild --clean`
# — it's cheap and deterministic from app.json, not something to keep
# around as tracked source.
/android
/ios

# Machine-local Expo state (device pairing history, dev server settings)
# — the other expo-doctor finding. Never useful to another machine or CI,
# and differs per developer.
.expo/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Native build artifacts (only relevant if android/ios are ever
# temporarily present locally — harmless to keep even though the whole
# folders are already excluded above)
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.orig.*

# Metro / bundler
.metro-health-check*

# Env files — never commit real secrets. .env.example stays tracked.
.env
.env.local

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Logs
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo

# EAS
.eas/
